{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 32, :comments ["<b>And whoever fills his hand</b> — for I might say this refers only to one anointed with the anointing oil; from where do I derive one invested with the additional garments? Scripture says: \"and whoever fills his hand (to don the garments).\" These are all the High Priests who served from Yoshiyahu onward, for in his days the flask of anointing oil was hidden away — this is the language of Rashi (Rashi on Leviticus 16:32). But the Rav's intent is not that there was no High Priest invested with the additional garments in the Temple from Yoshiyahu onward, for in the Gemara (Horayot 13a) they asked: one anointed with anointing oil and one invested with the additional garments — which of them takes precedence? And they said (Makkot 11a): does he [the accidental murderer] return [from his city of refuge] upon the death of all of them, or does he return upon the death of even one of them — [from which we infer that] all of them are found at the same time. Rather, in all periods, if one was invested with the additional garments he is fit for the service of Yom HaKippurim, for they always prepare another priest [as substitute] for Yom HaKippurim (Yoma 2a) and they do not anoint him, and if a disqualification befell the serving High Priest, this one serves in his stead, for he is qualified through the investiture of the garments without anointing."], :book :leviticus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {0 "The phrase 'ללבוש את הבגדים' appears in parentheses in the source, evidently a gloss inserted into the Hebrew text clarifying the intent of 'fills his hand.'"}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:54:40.832257260Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}